        "problem": "Calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x) = x\\sec x.$",
        "worked_solution": "We use the product rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xsec\u2061x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)\\cdot sec\u2061x+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(sec\u2061x) \\\\  & =(1)\\cdot sec\u2061x+x\\cdot (sec\u2061xtan\u2061x) \\\\  & =sec\u2061x(1+xtan\u2061x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
